  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "The velocity $v$ of a particle at time $t$ is given by $v(t)={e}^{2-3t}.$ Calculate the acceleration of the particle at time $t.$",
  "worked_solution": "We differentiate $v(t)$ to calculate $a(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2-3t}) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {e}^{2-3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
